# jobpipe schedule. Times are container-local (TZ=Asia/Kolkata, set in the
# Dockerfile), so these are IST and they do not drift.
#
# Weekdays only: applying on a Sunday morning puts you at the bottom of a
# Monday inbox.
#
# THE FULL RUN IS AT 14:00, NOT 07:00, AND THE TIME IS LOAD-BEARING.
# Google rolls the free-tier day at midnight America/Los_Angeles, which is
# 12:30 IST in PDT and 13:30 IST in PST. A 07:00 run sits on the PREVIOUS
# quota day, so it inherits whatever the previous evening already spent -- and
# on gemini-flash-latest, whose free cap is 20 calls a day, "whatever was
# already spent" is routinely all of it. 14:00 is past the boundary in both
# halves of the year, so the run always starts on a full quota. The queue is
# ready for the evening rather than the morning; that is the trade, and a full
# quota is worth more than the hour.
#
# min hour dom mon dow  command
   0  14    *   *  1-5  python -u -m jobpipe.cli daily

# `daily`, never the stages by hand. `ingest && score && prepare && notify` --
# what this line used to be -- has no budget sizing (prepare asks for 30 calls
# against a 20/day cap and dies halfway with 429s), no fallback when the tailor
# model is 503ing, and no pdf stage, which is how ten PDFs went missing on
# 2026-09-01. daily also runs track and readme-stats.

# Reply tracking is cheap, spends no LLM budget, and is worth running more
# often than the pipeline. These stay in the morning on purpose -- a reply that
# landed overnight is worth seeing with coffee.
   0   7    *   *  1-5  python -u -m jobpipe.cli track
   0  19    *   *  1-5  python -u -m jobpipe.cli track
